# Quorian

## Lore

The Quorians are an alien warrior people, called to the Palladium World by the Dwarves during the Elf-Dwarf War to be set against the Elves'' Gosai. They soon lost patience with the war and walked away from their summoners, but the feud with the Gosai outlived it and is still handed from parent to child thousands of years on. The Riftlords who knew the road back to Quoria died or vanished in the fighting, so the whole people is stranded, and a great many Quorians treat finding a way home as the work of a lifetime.

For all their love of a fight they keep their heads in battle, do not kill idly, and hold life dear, with the Gosai as the standing exception. Most earn their keep as wandering men at arms. Their pride is quick to take offense and is usually settled by a duel or a brawl, which among their own kind is survivable because of how fast they heal; the same gift makes them reckless, slow to retreat and contemptuous of armor. They are also deeply superstitious about dreams, and a single odd dream can turn a Quorian''s whole life in a new direction.

In recent generations more of them have settled. Oneiromancers found that the great hills of the wastelands are the burrows of sleeping Earthshakers and that the sleepers can be reached in dreams, so villages of a few hundred have grown up on top of them, with the rest of the community guarding the place. Nomads still travel in wandercamps of ten to sixty. Within a year of the first dream-vision a young Quorian leaves the family camp and by custom is never welcome back.

**Alignment:** Any, leaning very heavily toward the honorable ones: principled, scrupulous and aberrant.

**O.C.C.s available:** Any. Most are men at arms of some kind; wizardry and elemental magic are growing more common; Diabolism and Summoning are distrusted; clergy and psychic O.C.C.s are uncommon, and those with the gift usually become Oneiromancers.

**Physical Appearance:** Big, heavily built people. The eyes are solid red with no pupil to be seen, the skin a muted bluish violet, and the hair grows in thick cords that some gather behind the head.

**Size:** 6-7 feet (2 to 2.3 m). **Weight:** 200-300 lbs (91 to 136 kg).

**Average Life Span:** 50-60 years.

**Habitat:** Mostly the Baalgor Wastelands, with sightings in the Yin-Sloth Jungles, near Mount Nimro and in the Old Kingdom.

**Languages:** Their own tongue and Dwarven. Many also read and write and pick up Elven, Gobblely and Human dialects.

**Enemies:** The Gosai first of all, then giants, trolls, ogres, orcs and anyone standing between them and the way home or their devotion to the Earthshakers.

**Allies:** Eandroth, Dragonmen and humans in general. Cool toward Dwarves and Elves, indifferent to most others.

## GM Notes

Two habits drive a Quorian at the table. The first is the armor taboo: one who straps on a breastplate is shamed and can be cast out by other Quorians, though they do not judge other races by the same rule and are impressed by an opponent who faces them unarmored. The second is the reluctance to withdraw, since backing out of a fight, even for a good reason, can be read as cowardice.

Quorians had no priests before they came to this world, which is why they look to Shamans, Psi-Mystics and Oneiromancers rather than to clergy for the reading of dreams. Their legends hold that a few Riftlords survived and are waiting in secret to lead the people home.
